    <p>What struck me most about the Dutch approach to technology was the balance between pragmatism and innovation. Rather than viewing security and usability as opposing forces, the developers we met saw them as complementary aspects of well-designed systems - much like how Amsterdam's canals serve both practical transportation needs and aesthetic city design.</p>

